-- cancel: Xor (Xor e (Const k)) (Const k) becomes cancel e, ahead of the general clause
-- Xor a b ↦ Xor (cancel a) (cancel b). One pass computes, for each expression, its cancelled form
-- and the cancelled form of its left operand (for Xor u v, cancel u), so every recursive call is on a field.
inner : Expr → Expr
inner Input = Input
inner (Const b) = Const b
inner (Xor u v) = u
